./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:105:The achievable router captures most of the oracle's routing value but leaves a real gap that
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:116:| b    | router | conf-thresh | random | oracle | router−conf | router−random |
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:124:request_dependent, sigma=0.6 (noisier observables): router−conf grows to +0.016 .. +0.024.
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:126:uniform (null): all policies collapse onto each other (router−conf ≈ 0.000–0.001); only
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:127:random/oracle bracket trivially. As pre-committed, NO routing helps when degradation is uniform.
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:129:- vs all-quant / all-full: router DOMINATES both endpoints (strictly Pareto-better) ✅ in
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:132:- vs random@matched-b: router beats it decisively (+0.02 to +0.09 quality) ✅.
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:133:- vs CONFIDENCE-THRESHOLD@matched-b (the STRONG baseline): router wins, but the margin is
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:135:  (1000 resamples, results/bootstrap_router_vs_conf.csv):
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:137:  | sigma | mean Δ(router−conf) | 95% CI            | beats conf? |
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:143:ANSWER: The pre-decode router beats confidence-threshold at matched budget ONLY when the
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:144:post-decode confidence signal is at least as noisy as the pre-decode features (sigma>=0.3 here).
./experiments/2026-06-03/EXP-0020/committee1/systems_reviewer.err:145:At low noise (sigma=0.15) confidence-threshold TIES it (CI includes 0). The router NEVER loses,

