 succeeded in 0ms:
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/torchao.md:3:TorchAO is an architecture optimization library for PyTorch, it provides high performance dtypes, optimization techniques and kernels for inference and training, featuring composability with native PyTorch features like torch.compile, FSDP etc.. Some benchmark numbers can be found [here](https://github.com/pytorch/ao/tree/main/torchao/quantization#benchmarks).
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/torchao.md:17:You can quantize your own huggingface model with torchao, e.g. [transformers](https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/quantization/torchao) and [diffusers](https://huggingface.co/docs/diffusers/en/quantization/torchao), and save the checkpoint to huggingface hub like [this](https://huggingface.co/jerryzh168/llama3-8b-int8wo) with the following example code:
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/torchao.md:24:    from torchao.quantization import Int8WeightOnlyConfig
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/torchao.md:27:    quantization_config = TorchAoConfig(Int8WeightOnlyConfig())
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/torchao.md:32:        quantization_config=quantization_config
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/llm_compressor.md:4:It provides a comprehensive set of quantization algorithms, including support for techniques such as FP4, FP8, INT8, and INT4 quantization.
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/llm_compressor.md:17:LLM Compressor handles the complexity of quantization, calibration, and format conversion, producing models ready for immediate use with vLLM.
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/llm_compressor.md:21:- **Multiple Quantization Algorithms**: Support for AWQ, GPTQ, AutoRound, and Round-to-Nearest.
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/llm_compressor.md:22:Also includes support for QuIP and SpinQuant-style transforms as well as KV cache and attention quantization.
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/llm_compressor.md:23:- **Multiple Quantization Methods**: Support for FP8, INT8, INT4, NVFP4, MXFP4, and mixed-precision quantization
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/quantized_kvcache.md:3:## FP8 KV Cache Overview
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/quantized_kvcache.md:5:Efficient memory usage is crucial for working with large language models. Quantizing the KV (Key-Value) cache to FP8 format can significantly reduce its memory footprint. This optimization enables you to store more tokens in memory, leading to improved throughput and support for longer context windows.
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/quantized_kvcache.md:7:> **Note:** When using the Flash Attention 3 backend with FP8 KV cache, attention operations are also performed in the quantized (FP8) domain. In this configuration, queries are quantized to FP8 in addition to keys and values.
/tmp/vllm-claim0015-83328/docs/features/quantization/quantized_kvcache.md:9:### Supported FP8 KV-Cache Quantization Schemes
